Z||000000||dantheman1998||10-23-2001||10:06 PM||||i have a 450 hp engine that i am going to bie<BR>. now all i need is a fiero. what fiero will hold up to this power? will the th-125 hold power?i have heard of a 125 -c what is that?<BR>the trans has to hold up to 1/4 racing. do they make torque converters for this trans?what is the best year fiero and model for the lowest amount of money?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Spektrum-87GT||10-23-2001||10:25 PM||||i dont think any stock automatic transaxle is going to be able to handle 450hp. the 5 speed getrag will according to archie(www.v8archie.com) but i dont know about for 1/4 mile racing. <P>now, the second question can vary widely. do you want looks? stictly performance? you can pick up an 84 for dirt cheap(i've seen them go for 100 bucks) or you can get an 85 gt(or 86/87 se) they look better and dont weight much(if any) more, they do cost more though. My recommendation would be an 87 or 88 gt. they have the getrag 5 speeds and (in my opinion) are the best looking fieros by far. as far as price? i've seen ones with blown engines go for less than 1000. one thing i've learned... if you're going to mod a fiero, you cant be cheap or it will turn out bad, and most fiero owners(me included) are just that... cheap... we squeek when we walk  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroKyle||10-23-2001||10:55 PM||||I don't consider myself cheap.... I have always had the motto, if its more expensive, its more thank likely better. Not always true, but most of the time.<P>Thats one thing you can't cut corners on trying to high performance a Fiero is on costs and what it takes to get it right.<P>I reccomend to e-mail or private message Archie. He might have some great advice. He is the Fiero V-8 King.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dave Gunsul||10-23-2001||11:59 PM||||That's excellent advise from Fierokyle above!<BR>We have two Fieros in our club that are running 450 HP 350's in them with no problems<BR>all thanks to Archie!<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||14
